</li><li> Faction
</li></ul>


== TLDR; Walkthrough ==

* You need amiable or higher faction with [[Clurg_(NPC)|Clurg]]. The most common way for non-ogres to attain this is to be a level 8+ Dark Elf Enchanter or level 12+ Enchanter of any race.
* '''Get [[Kiola Nut]]'''
** Go to [[Ocean of Tears]]. Turn into a Wood Elf and/or cast faction spell on [[Cleonae Kalen]] (located at "Sisters Island") to purchase a [[Kiola Nut]] 
* '''Get [[Honey Jum]]'''
** Get 3 [[Honeycomb]]s by killing Bixies of any kind ([[a Bixie]]) in [[Kithicor Forest]] or [[Misty Thicket]].  Kith seems to be better drop rate.
** Go to [[Rivervale]].  Turn into a Gnome and/or cast faction spell on [[Kizzie Mintopp]] then give her the 30GP (must be gold) and three [[Honeycomb]]s, to receive the [[Honey Jum]]
* '''Get [[Erud's Tonic]]'''
** Purchase [[Innoruuk's Kiss of Death]] from vendors in [[Erudin]] (recommended and faster) or in [[Freeport]].  Cast Human or Erudite illusion and/or faction spell if needed to buy the item.  
** Go to [[Erudin]]. Turn into Human or Erudite and/or cast faction spell on [[Sinnkin Highbrow]] (3rd floor of library), give her the [[Innoruuk's Kiss of Death]] to receive [[Erud's Tonic]]
* '''Get [[Koalindl Fish]] (the easy way while avoiding brutal Qeynos faction hits)'''
** Create an alt Warrior as a "The Prime Healer" worshiper and throw all of the points into stamina, the home city will be [[Qeynos]].  Go to guild master and put skill points into 1hs and kick and level the warrior up to level 2, equip any cloth armor you get killing trash during this time.  When you hit level 2 put more skill points into 1hs and kick etc. to be more effective in killing the 2 fish in the pool.
** Take your Enchanter to [[Qeynos]] and camp them by the pool where the fish spawn
** Login on an alt warrior and kill fish in the pool until one has a [[Koalindl Fish]] on the corpse.  Login on Enchanter and loot [[Koalindl Fish]]. (Tip: having someone else hail the 2 pathing NPC's and hold them up from getting around the pool helps. They will assist the fish and 1 shot kill you) (Another tip: I've been able to kill the fish with unskilled level 1 characters before. You do have to get lucky though on the hit rolls, but if you're lazy it may be worth to try).
**NOTE: I just make a Human Monk and start in [[Qeynos]], spend my 5 skill up on 1h Blunt and use the newb note quest. Can easy kill the fish without too much of a hard time, kick is better on a monk than a warrior at that level.
**Alternatively you can kill [[Frostbite]] at the Barbarian fishing village in [[Western Karana]] right near the [[Qeynos Hills]] zone line. Beware of the patrolling Barbarian as they may assist.

* '''Get [[Barkeep Compendium]]''' 
** Go to [[Freeport]]. Turn into a Human and/or cast faction spell on [[Gregor Nasin]] (at East Freeport docks). Give [[Gregor Nasin]] the [[Kiola Nut]], [[Honey Jum]], [[Koalindl Fish]], and [[Erud's Tonic]] all at the same time and receive the [[Barkeep Compendium]]

* '''Get [[Stein of Moggok]]'''
** Go to [[Oggok]]. Turn into a Dark Elf or Ogre and/or cast faction spell on [[Clurg]] (located around area 17 of the [[Oggok]] map). Give him the [[Barkeep Compendium]] to receive the [[Stein of Moggok]]


Enjoy your Stein!  '''<u>Also, if you are trying to do this multiple times remember that the Stein is Lore so DO NOT have one on you when you turn in the [[Barkeep Compendium]].</u>''' Many hearts have been broken because people tried to do this quest while already possessing a Stein and seeing they do not receive a 2nd Stein upon quest completion :)

